                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is a fairly average rpg with a base builder twist. The pathmaking & ai are pretty bad at times - sometimes the enemy will get stuck behind an obstacle or cliff instead of going around it. Similarly, if you set your character to aggressive with a bow, they will keep firing at an enemy behind a wall even if the enemy is unreachable. The graphics for the time of release are ok. The base builder setup is simple but good where you can build barracks for troop production, towers for defense & research a bit of tech. The loot drops are fairly random - the bow I found in the first cave in the second hour of my playthrough was stronger than some of the weapons that dropped at the end of the game. I did experience one bug when I first started the game & played the tutorial mode, then tried to exit the game but it froze. After that the game played well from then on. There is some replay as a mode can be unlocked after completing the campaign.\n\nI would give this game a slight recommendation if you are a fan of rpgs, especially if it is on sale.",
